<h1>point access method</h1>
<p>
(definition)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
A data structure and associated algorithms primarily to search for points defined in multidimensional space.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Also known as</strong> PAM.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Specialization</strong> (... is a kind of me.)<br>
<a href="excell.html"><em>EXCELL</em></a>, <a href="gridfile.html"><em>grid file</em></a>, <a href="hbtree.html"><em>hB-tree</em></a>, <a href="twingridfl.html"><em>twin grid file</em></a>, <a href="twolevgrid.html"><em>two-level grid file</em></a>, <a href="kdtree.html"><em>k-d tree</em></a>, <a href="bsptree.html"><em>BSP-tree</em></a>, <a href="quadtree.html"><em>quadtree</em></a>, <a href="ubtree.html"><em>UB-tree</em></a>, <a href="buddytree.html"><em>buddy tree</em></a>, <a href="localitySensitiveHashing.html"><em>locality-sensitive hashing</em></a>.
</p>
<p>
<strong>See also</strong>
<a href="spatialAccessMethod.html"><em>spatial access method</em></a>, <a href="spaceOrderingMethod.html"><em>space ordering method</em></a>.
</p>

<p>
<em>Note:
After <a href="../terms.html#GG98">[GG98]</a>.</em>
</p>

<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorPEB">PEB</a></p>

